<title>BELGIUM: EU reviews Siemens stake in Huelsbeck.</title>
<headline>EU reviews Siemens stake in Huelsbeck.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had started a routine probe into Siemens's proposed acquisition of a stake in Huelsbeck &amp; Fuerst GmbH, a German maker of car locking systems.</p>
<p>Siemens announced in January it was buying 25 percent of Huelsbeck, a family-owned company with 600 million marks in 1996 sales.</p>
<p>The Commission said the deal was notified for clearance on March 21 under the EU's merger rules which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions. It has about a month from that date to clear the operation or start a full probe.</p>
<p>Siemens has numerous activities in the industrial and electronic sectors, including technology for cars.</p>
<p>-- Amelia Torres 322 2876841</p>
</text>
